\f1\fs22 \'93What happened?\'94 Director Hardman yelled at the hologram.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93We have been conducting some preliminary experiments in viral gene transfer. It is very interesting, Director. We know our predecessors used tardigrade DNA to horizontally transfer plant and algae genes and we have had remarkable success in replicating their processes. The genes, they, they transfer so easily, the possibilities are limitless. It is an astonishing field of research. Paths previously blocked are now open.\'94 Dr Kitsen was speaking way too fast for Damien to keep up. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You are babbling doctor, what happened?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93We tested new prototype pathogen. Our calculations assured us that no-one was in danger.\'94 The nervous junior geneticist stuttered. \'93It killed every red-head in the room.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Anyone I know?\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I would not think so, sir. They were just random lows.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Document the experiment and safely store the pathogen.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Don\'92t you want us to destroy it?\'94 Dr Kitsen hoped so. His flame haired wife would not be happy to know he was behind a Ranga Holocaust.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93No, it might have some commercial value in the future.\'94 Director Hardman did not want to lose an opportunity to create a valuable weapon. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93But it only targets redheads.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes.\'94 The Director imagined a world without redheads and concluded they wouldn\'92t be missed. 
\f2\i Freckles and orange pubes? Alabaster skin that turns to cancer under the glare of a 50 watt bulb? 
\f1\i0 He visibly shuddered. \'93Continue with your experiments, I want you well practiced when the samples arrive. We will be on a tight schedule when the time comes, but in the meantime please conduct no further tests on live subjects.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes, Director.\'94\

